      <ThreadGroup guiclass="ThreadGroupGui" testclass="ThreadGroup" testname="Habitat edit contention @ 2 user(s)">
        <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">2 thread(s) editing DIFFERENT habitats in the SAME project.

runUpdate sets lock_timeout to 5s then takes SELECT … FOR UPDATE on the
project row, so these serialise and eventually 409 with &quot;Another edit for
this project is in progress&quot;. The number to read is the 409 RATE, not the
latency — 409 is a correct answer here, so it is asserted as acceptable
and counted separately in the summary rather than painting the report red.</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">${__P(users_editContention_2,2)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">1</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.scheduler">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.duration">${__P(window_editContention_2,8)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.delay">${__P(delay_editContention_2,865)}</stringProp>
