      <!-- Single-project fetch ramp -->
      <ThreadGroup guiclass="ThreadGroupGui" testclass="ThreadGroup" testname="Single-project fetch ramp (1 user, one size after another)">
        <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">GET /projects/{id} at each staged document size, one user.

The list endpoints have a bounded payload and a SizeAssertion to prove it
(BMD-933 AC1). This one returns the entire project document and is what
every habitat-list page load pulls, with no pagination above it. One user
so the number is the payload cost, not a contention cost.

Loop-count driven inside a duration guard, like the size ramp: each size
gets an exact sample count, and a size with no staged project runs zero
loops rather than GETting /projects/ with an empty path segment.</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">${__P(users_fetchRamp,1)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">1</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.scheduler">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.duration">${__P(window_fetchRamp,27)}</stringProp>
