      <!-- Mixed workload -->
      <ThreadGroup guiclass="ThreadGroupGui" testclass="ThreadGroup" testname="Mixed workload (reads + edits + uploads together)">
        <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">A weighted mix of everything, run concurrently rather than in phases.

Every staircase in this plan proves an operation scales on its own. This
group is the one that asks whether they scale TOGETHER — the same pool,
the same database, at the same time. Weights are MIX_*_PERCENT and should
add up to 100; they are percent-of-iterations, so they do not drift with
how fast each endpoint happens to be.

WINDOW_mixed stretches this group on its own — long enough for a leak,
a growing session store or pool exhaustion to show up, none of which a
30-second phase can see.

The edit and revalidate slices deliberately share the prepared pool, so
a project is being edited while it is being re-validated. That is safe
to repeat: carry-forward-feature-ids.js keys featureIds by parcel ref,
so re-validating the same file into the same project reuses the ids the
edit slice is reading from the CSV rather than minting new ones. Without
that, every revalidate would 404 the edits behind it.</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">${__P(users_mixed,8)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">1</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.scheduler">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.duration">${__P(window_mixed,120)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.delay">${__P(delay_mixed,933)}</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.same_user_on_next_iteration">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.on_sample_error">continue</stringProp>
        <elementProp name="ThreadGroup.main_controller" elementType="LoopController" guiclass="LoopControlPanel" testclass="LoopController" testname="Loop Controller">
          <stringProp name="LoopController.loops">-1</stringProp>
          <boolProp name="LoopController.continue_forever">true</boolProp>
        </elementProp>
      </ThreadGroup>
